The editors of [KUYBGM7V] suggest as author of the two works the 13th-century gSang phu ba bSod nams rin chen mchog.</note></person></listPerson><listBibl><bibl xml:id="work3727"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bodhicaryāvatāra</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byang chub sems dpa'i spyod pa la 'jug pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">spyod 'jug</title><date type="composition" notBefore="0610-01-01" notAfter="0800-12-31">after 610 before 800</date><author ref="person:3743">śāntideva</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">A fragmentary manuscript of the Tibetan translation (different from the canonical one) from Matho is discussed in [5H5BVSWI].</note><idno type="APIS">3727</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work4647"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byang chub sems pa'i bslabs pa kun las btus pa'i don bsdus pa</title><title xml:lang="bo">བྱང་ཆུབ་སེམས་པའི་བསླབས་པ་ཀུན་ལས་བཏུས་པའི་དོན་བསྡུས་པ</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byang chub seMs pa'i bslabs pa kun las btus pa'i don bsdus pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byang chub skyabs kyis mdzad pa'i bslab btus pa'i don bsdus pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bslab btus kyi sa bcad</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1110-01-01" notAfter="1237-12-31">after 1110 before 1237</date><author ref="person:3864">'jad pa byang chub skyabs</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">Topical outline of the Śikṣāsamuccaya (ID:3742). The author also wrote a commentary on that work, see (ID:4649).</note><idno type="APIS">4647</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work4649"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byang chub sems dpa' yi bslabs pa kun las btus pa'i 'grel bshad</title><title xml:lang="bo">བྱང་ཆུབ་སེམས་དཔའ་ཡི་བསླབས་པ་ཀུན་ལས་བཏུས་པའི་འགྲེལ་བཤད</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byang chub sems dpa' yi bslabs pa kun las btus pa'i 'grel bshad</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byang chub skyabs kyis mdzad pa'i bslab pa kun btus kyi rnam bshad</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byang chub sems dpa'i bslab pa kun las btus pa'i 'grel bshad rin chen sgron me</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1110-01-01" notAfter="1237-12-31">after 1110 before 1237</date><author ref="person:3864">'jad pa byang chub skyabs</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">Commentary on the Śikṣāsamuccaya (ID:3742). The author also wrote a topical outline of that work, see (ID:4647).&#13;
&#13;
The author refers to the views of his predecessors, some of whom are identified in glosses in (ID:4648), for instance lo tsa ba (ID:3786), Phya pa (ID:3831), Zhang tshes (ID:3805).&#13;
&#13;
The discussion on "dgos 'brel" bears a close similarity to that found in the works of Phya pa, speaking in favor of the author being his student 'Jad pa Byang chub skyabs.</note><idno type="APIS">4649</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5147"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byang chub sems dpa'i spyod pa la 'jug pa'i rnam par bshad pa</title><title xml:lang="bo">བྱང་ཆུབ་སེམས་དཔའི་སྤྱོད་པ་ལ་འཇུག་པའི་རྣམ་པར་བཤད་པ</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1110-01-01" notAfter="1237-12-31">after 1110 before 1237</date><author ref="person:3864">'jad pa byang chub skyabs</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">The author uses some Sanskrit words rather than their Tibetan equivalents (e.g., bud+d+ha, loka).&#13;
The passage on "purpose and connection" (dgos 'brel) (see (ID:5146), fol. 5b) is quasi identical (albeit a bit shorter) to the one in a Śikṣāsamuccaya commentary (ID:4649) also by "byang chub skyabs," lending support to the author of both works being the same.&#13;
